    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround mini.align etc\n\n### Description\n\nI notice that many mini modules hard code the `help message delay` to 1 second:\r\n\r\nfor example:\r\n\r\n- **mini.surround**:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/690a3b4c78c4956f7ecf770124b522d32084b872/lua/mini/surround.lua#L1948\r\n\r\n- **mini.align**:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/690a3b4c78c4956f7ecf770124b522d32084b872/lua/mini/align.lua#L1794\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nI am aware that many modules can be configured with `silent = true`, this is equivalent to setting `delay = ∞`\r\n\r\nusers have to choose `delay = 1000` or `delay = ∞`, but they might prefer other values\r\n\r\nwould you be willing to add an option to allow the delay to be configurable?",
