        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "This is my personal preference.  \n\nI like instant feedback (`delay=0`) or no feedback at all (`delay=∞`).  \n\nI feel anxious in the following two situations:  \n\n1. When I haven't pressed any key, but information appears on the screen.  \n2. If I happen to finish pressing a key slightly over one second, the feedback message will flash briefly, causing the screen to flicker.  \n\nWith a delay of one second, these two situations occur quite frequently...  \n\nMoreover, when I first started using mini, I mistakenly thought mini was so slow that I needed to wait one second for feedback (I didn’t read the help file carefully).  \n\nFor these reasons, I believe adding a `delay` option is necessary—at least allowing the choice of `delay=0`.",
